<task id="126" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H4: real value-sourcing per KvSecretValueSource (generate/copy/reference) + task-084 canonical manifest DI-swap (C2.2)</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-2 -- Entry + resources</phase>
    <gate>cleared</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>THE top-priority correctness fix in the whole Wave G build per DS-4 -- currently writes literal placeholder VALUES to Key Vault, silently breaking every downstream secret consumer. FULL rigor, highest scrutiny.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Named explicitly in the parent task instructions' xhigh-effort exception list: 'complex brownfield (H4 real-values migration)' -- Sonnet @ xhigh.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>125</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, job-handler, auth, config</tags>
    <estimated-effort>10-16 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Fix the SECOND, more dangerous half of H4's defect (DS-4 §3: 'What it did NOT surface: the writer's placeholder secret VALUES... mean a successful H4 leaves every downstream secret consumer broken'). AzCliKvSecretsWriter.ResolveValueForEntry (AzCliKvSecretsWriter.cs:223) currently writes literal '{name}-interim-placeholder-{customerId}' VALUES for every KV secret entry -- H4 can report Success while every downstream consumer (H3's app-reg secret reads, H6's SolutionImport:ClientSecret, H7's EnvVarValues:ClientSecret, H14's cert reads) silently receives a non-functional string. Implement REAL value-sourcing per the existing KvSecretValueSource enum (generate/copy/reference): generate = cryptographically random secret generation for entries that are genuinely new secrets; copy = read-and-copy from an existing source (e.g., a platform-level secret being propagated to the customer stamp); reference = a KV-reference pointer to another vault's secret (no value copy, just the reference wiring). ALSO perform the task-084 canonical manifest DI-swap (C2.2, a 1-line change per DS-4): replace the interim StaticKvSecretManifest binding (Program.cs:328) with the already-built canonical manifest from task 084 (Phase H, already shipped per TASK-INDEX.md).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in secret-value provisioning strategies (generate/copy/reference), cryptographically secure random generation, and safe manifest-driven KV population.</role>

  <goal>For every KvSecretValueSource.Generate entry, H4 writes a real cryptographically-random value (not a placeholder string). For every KvSecretValueSource.Copy entry, H4 reads the actual source value and copies it. For every KvSecretValueSource.Reference entry, H4 wires a KV reference (not a value copy). The 1-line manifest DI-swap replaces StaticKvSecretManifest with the task-084 canonical manifest. A downstream-consumer smoke test (e.g., H3 or H7 reading a value H4 wrote) confirms the value is FUNCTIONAL, not a placeholder string.

  **Auth-v4 coordination amendment (v3.5, 2026-08-19, per spec.md FR-39)**: "real value" for the `BFF-API-ClientSecret` manifest entry specifically now includes a THIRD acceptable outcome beyond generate/copy/reference: **already-migrated-to-FIC**. If the manifest entry (or a run-time flag coordinated with `spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI`) indicates the target customer BFF's OBO credential is FIC-based rather than secret-based, H4 MUST NOT generate a secret value for that entry -- instead it either OMITS the KV secret entirely or writes a documented sentinel value (exact contract TBD with auth-v4; do not invent the sentinel format unilaterally -- coordinate per the transition schedule in `notes/AUTH-V4-CHANGE-REQUEST-RESPONSE.md`). This is additive to the existing generate/copy/reference branches -- it does not change their behavior for any OTHER KV secret.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 calls this 'the top-priority correctness fix' in the entire handler-build backlog: 'Placeholder VALUES silently break downstream handlers.' DS-4 §3 (H4 deep-dive) is explicit that POML 047 (the original H4 task) HONESTLY DISCLOSED the interim manifest binding as a documented Path A exception, but did NOT surface the placeholder-VALUES defect -- meaning even a fully-informed reviewer of the original work would not have caught this without reading AzCliKvSecretsWriter.cs:223 directly, which DS-4's grep-verified audit did. Task 084 (Phase H, already ✅ per TASK-INDEX.md) already built the canonical secret-catalog manifest generator -- this task's manifest-swap half is literally a 1-line DI change per DS-4's own sizing.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/SecretClientKvWriter.cs (task 125's output -- this task fixes ResolveValueForEntry inside it)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/KvSecretValueResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Program.cs (or .Worker/.Api Program.cs post-split -- the 1-line manifest DI swap, Program.cs:328 pre-split line reference)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/KvSecretValueSource.cs (existing enum)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/ (task 084's manifest generator output)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="125" status="pending">The SDK-ported SecretClientKvWriter this task's value-resolution fix modifies must exist</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-38">L2's admin-env Dataverse credential model is Path X: L2 UAMI registered as a Dataverse Application User via DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the UAMI (DS-8). MUST NOT provision a new client-secret for L2. The Dataverse-ClientSecret KV secret itself MUST NOT be deleted (BFF still consumes it) -- only L2's dependency on it is removed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §3 H4 deep-dive">This task's fix MUST land TOGETHER with the 1-line manifest DI-swap (C2.2) in the same wave -- per DS-4's own note: 'Under Option D: SecretClient + real value-sourcing + task-084 canonical manifest swap (C2.2, 1 line) land together.'</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §9 Security Rules">Generated secret values MUST use a cryptographically secure random generator (System.Security.Cryptography, not System.Random). Generated/copied values MUST NEVER be logged (grep the implementation for any Log* call that could include the secret value).</constraint>
    <constraint source="this project's spec.md FR-35/FR-36">Canonical KV secret naming applies to every entry this resolver writes -- verify against task-084's manifest schema, not a hand-maintained name list.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-39 (added v3.5 2026-08-19, per auth-v4 coordination)">For the `BFF-API-ClientSecret` manifest entry specifically, coordinate the exact "already-migrated-to-FIC" contract (omit vs sentinel value, and the sentinel's format if used) with `spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI` per the phased-rollout schedule in `notes/AUTH-V4-CHANGE-REQUEST-RESPONSE.md` -- do not ship a unilateral sentinel format without cross-checking it is what auth-v4's BFF-side code will actually look for (or ignore).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H4 real value-sourcing + canonical manifest swap</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Generate/copy/reference value sourcing" location="src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/KvSecretValueSource.cs">The existing enum already models the 3 sourcing strategies; this task is the first REAL implementation behind it -- all 3 branches are currently placeholder-string regardless of the entry's declared source type.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL, xhigh effort). Read AzCliKvSecretsWriter.cs:223's ResolveValueForEntry in full, KvSecretValueSource.cs's enum definition, and task-084's canonical manifest schema.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Manifest swap first">Perform the 1-line DI swap: replace StaticKvSecretManifest with the task-084 canonical manifest binding. Verify H4 still resolves the SAME (or a superset/correctly-updated) entry list post-swap.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Generate branch">Implement cryptographically secure random generation (RandomNumberGenerator) for KvSecretValueSource.Generate entries, respecting each entry's declared length/character-set constraints if the manifest specifies them.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Copy branch">Implement the read-and-copy path for KvSecretValueSource.Copy entries -- read the actual source value (platform KV or another documented source per the manifest) and write it to the customer stamp's KV.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Reference branch">Implement the KV-reference wiring for KvSecretValueSource.Reference entries -- no value copy, just the reference pointer per the manifest's declared target.</step>
    <step order="5" name="No-log guard">Audit the resolver for any logging call that could include a resolved secret VALUE (names/keys are fine to log per existing convention; values are NEVER logged) -- fix any violation found.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Downstream smoke">Author or extend an integration test where a downstream consumer (e.g., a fake H3/H7-shaped reader) reads a value H4 wrote and confirms it is NOT the '{name}-interim-placeholder-{customerId}' pattern -- this is the regression net for the exact defect DS-4 found.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the task-084 canonical manifest's schema does not actually specify enough information to resolve a Copy or Reference entry (e.g., no declared source vault/secret name for a Copy-type entry), STOP and escalate to the manifest's owner (task 084) rather than inventing a source ad hoc — a wrong-but-silent source resolution is exactly the class of defect this task exists to eliminate, applied one level up.</trigger>
    <trigger>Auth-v4 coordination (spec.md FR-39): if `spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI`'s Phase 5 (secret retirement) lands BEFORE this task executes -- i.e., `BFF-API-ClientSecret` is no longer provisioned anywhere in the auth-v4 rollout -- STOP and escalate to the project owner. Drop `BFF-API-ClientSecret` handling from this task's scope entirely rather than implementing generate/copy/reference/sentinel branching for a secret that no longer has a live consumer.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build/test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/KvSecretValueResolver.cs</output>
    <output type="code">Program.cs (manifest DI-swap, 1 line)</output>
    <output type="test">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/KvSecretValueResolverTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'interim-placeholder' across the H4 collaborator files returns 0 matches post-fix.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test for a Generate-type entry confirms the written value is NOT deterministic/predictable (two consecutive resolutions produce DIFFERENT values, proving real randomness, not a fixed placeholder).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test for a Copy-type entry confirms the written value MATCHES the actual source value (not a placeholder derived from the entry name).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test for a Reference-type entry confirms a KV-reference pointer is wired, with no value-copy call made.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'StaticKvSecretManifest' in the active Program.cs DI registration returns 0 matches (task-084 canonical manifest bound instead).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A downstream-consumer smoke test confirms a value H4 wrote is functional (not matching the '{name}-interim-placeholder-{customerId}' pattern).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test for the `BFF-API-ClientSecret` entry under the "already-migrated-to-FIC" condition confirms H4 either omits the KV secret or writes the documented sentinel (per the coordinated contract) -- NOT a generated placeholder-shaped or random secret value.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- the KvSecretValueSource enum + task-084's canonical manifest already exist; only the RESOLUTION LOGIC behind the enum is placeholder. Extension -- implementing the 3 branches behind the existing enum, and swapping the 1-line manifest binding to the already-built canonical manifest, is the exact minimal-and-correct extension DS-4 prescribes. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- DS-4's own words: 'a successful H4 leaves every downstream secret consumer broken' -- H3 (app-reg secret reads), H6 (SolutionImport:ClientSecret), H7 (EnvVarValues:ClientSecret), and H14 (cert reads) would all receive non-functional placeholder strings while H4 itself reports Success, making this THE single highest-priority correctness gap in the entire Phase G'' build per DS-4's own explicit ranking.

  COMPLETION NOTES (2026-08-19): All 4 KvSecretValueSource branches implemented with REAL resolution (Generated = RandomNumberGenerator 256-bit hex; FromExistingKvSecret + FromRunParameters = real copy via a new KvSecretWriteRequest.SecretParameters seam keyed by canonical name, reading real cleartext via SecretClient.GetSecretAsync; FromBicepOutput = skip-if-already-present, else an HONEST Failed result -- no fabricated value). Manifest DI-swap: NEW FileKvSecretManifest.cs (task 084's manifest.yaml never had a .NET reader -- this was genuinely new work, not the assumed 1-line change; YamlDotNet 18.1.0 added, 0 CVEs). FR-39 FIC-omit seam added (KvSecretWriteRequest.OmitCanonicalNames, run-parameter-driven, no hardcoded name check). grep-verified: 0 'interim-placeholder' matches in live collaborator files (retired AzCliKvSecretsWriter.cs excluded, unregistered dead code); 0 'StaticKvSecretManifest' matches in Program.cs. L2 suite: 883 -> 903 (+20 tests), zero regressions. FLAGGED OPERATIONAL GAP (see notes/task-126-deviations.md Deviation #3): FromBicepOutput entries (~15 of 26 manifest entries) have no reachable source today -- customer.bicep never got the kv-secrets.generated.bicep module wired in (task 086's actual landed scope was narrower than that). A fresh customer run will hit QuarantineRequired on these entries until a follow-on task closes that gap. This is the CORRECT fail-loud behavior per DS-4's own mandate, not a regression -- but needs owner attention before Wave G-2 is called deployable.</notes>

  <execution>
